  "term": "basal magnocellular nucleus",
  "definition": "The basal magnocellular nucleus is a nucleus in the basal forebrain that sends broadly distributed projections to sensory and motor areas of the cortex. In this source, it did not project to the prelimbic/infralimbic prefrontal cortex and had weaker effects on cortical whisker-response activity than stimulation of the horizontal diagonal band of Broca.",
